    "description": "A product-catalog service stores roughly two million articles in PostgreSQL, with read replicas, a Redis view cache and an Elasticsearch index kept in sync. Domain code for pricing and assortment curates article objects, but right now it also contains raw SQL, session handling and cache keys, which is why 30 test doubles still speak SQL. The storage layout changes twice a year (a new read replica, a switch to a document index for the search path) and every change ripples through the domain services. The team wants domain code to ask for articles in domain terms and to keep all persistence knowledge in one place, so the storage technology can be replaced behind a stable interface. The decision to implement: how to mediate between domain objects and the store so clients work in collection-like domain queries instead of SQL.",
    "decision_statement": "Mediate between domain objects and the store behind a collection-like interface so storage details never reach clients.",
    "notes": "Identity-map is acceptable supporting evidence for the identity/caching axis."
  },
